WEBVTT

00:00:01.560 --> 00:00:27.520
"Leave It to Beaver" starring Barbara Billingsley, Hugh Beaumont, Tony Dow, and Jerry Mathers as the Beaver.

00:00:39.600 --> 00:00:45.080
Well, we're rather quiet tonight, don't you think a little, uh, pleasant conversation would add to our enjoyment of dinner?

00:00:45.080 --> 00:00:48.200
Yeah, I guess it would, Dad, but it cuts down on your eating time.

00:00:48.200 --> 00:00:54.870
Whose role happened at your school, Wally?

00:00:54.870 --> 00:00:59.960
Mr. Bromley, our science teacher, showed us some color slides that he took in Washington last summer.

00:01:00.220 --> 00:01:02.140
Well, what were they like?

00:01:02.140 --> 00:01:07.080
Well, um, he had stuff like Mrs. Bromley in front of the Senate building and, uh,

00:01:07.080 --> 00:01:11.960
and Mrs. Bromley in front of the Washington Monument and Mrs. Bromley in front of the White House.

00:01:11.960 --> 00:01:13.990
What do you think of our nation's capital?

00:01:13.990 --> 00:01:17.970
Well, um, I guess if you took Mrs. Bromley out of it, it'd be okay.

00:01:21.700 --> 00:01:26.750
Beaver, you're storing food in your cheek there like a squirrel.

00:01:26.750 --> 00:01:30.000
Sure, Mom, by doing it this way, I get more mileage out of one mouthful.

00:01:30.600 --> 00:01:33.560
- Never mind the mileage beaver, just eat properly.

00:01:33.560 --> 00:01:35.580
- Yes, sir.

00:01:35.580 --> 00:01:39.370
- Oh dear, anything interesting happen around here today?

00:01:39.370 --> 00:01:42.930
- Well, I had a letter from Margaret Bannerman.

00:01:42.930 --> 00:01:45.190
Her daughter Kitty was in your class a few years ago,

00:01:45.190 --> 00:01:48.710
Wally, you remember her, don't you?

00:01:48.710 --> 00:01:52.380
- Um, yeah, yeah, I remember her.

00:01:52.380 --> 00:01:56.480
She was a girl, and I think I got a couple letters

00:01:56.480 --> 00:01:57.590
from her last summer.

00:01:57.590 --> 00:02:00.000
- Margaret and her daughter are coming back to Mayfield

00:02:00.000 --> 00:02:01.860
to visit the grandmother this weekend.

00:02:01.860 --> 00:02:04.480
And guess what, Wally?

00:02:04.480 --> 00:02:05.980
- Um, what?

00:02:07.500 --> 00:02:09.380
- Mrs. Bannerman wants you to take Kitty

00:02:09.380 --> 00:02:11.380
to the dance at the Mayfield Country Club

00:02:11.380 --> 00:02:12.450
this Saturday night.

00:02:15.680 --> 00:02:16.570
- What's the matter, Wally?

00:02:16.570 --> 00:02:18.020
Don't you like Mom's carrots?

00:02:18.020 --> 00:02:19.260
You're turning kinda green.

00:02:21.070 --> 00:02:23.590
- Something wrong, son?

00:02:23.590 --> 00:02:27.700
- Um, well, um, I think the basketball coach

00:02:27.700 --> 00:02:30.000
