00:02:31.530 --> 00:02:34.270
Oh, Wally, couldn't you skip it and take Kitty to the dance?

00:02:34.890 --> 00:02:37.970
After all, before they moved, the Bannermans were our best friends.

00:02:39.170 --> 00:02:43.910
Well, gee, no, Mom, because if I do, the coach might cut me or something.

00:02:45.390 --> 00:02:47.200
That's a shame.

00:02:48.310 --> 00:02:50.760
Yeah, boy, that sure is a shame, all right.

00:02:52.960 --> 00:02:54.360
Can I be excused now, Dad?

00:02:55.050 --> 00:02:55.950
Yeah, I suppose so.

00:02:56.330 --> 00:02:57.340
Don't you want your dessert?

00:02:58.590 --> 00:03:00.000
Oh, no, thanks.

00:03:00.000 --> 00:03:02.850
Mama, I kind of want to get an early start on my homework

00:03:05.010 --> 00:03:12.390
Can you imagine that a boy preferring homework to dessert?

00:03:14.180 --> 00:03:21.400
Beaver if you eat that slowly you never will finish she did if I eat too fast I get yelled at and if it's too slow

00:03:21.400 --> 00:03:22.860
I get yelled at

00:03:22.860 --> 00:03:30.000
Are you by any chance trying to be annoying? Oh, no, sir. I'm not trying to be annoying. Let's just coming out that way

00:03:30.000 --> 00:03:43.930
oh dear you're a very helpful husband oh it's my pleasure you remember the first time you helped

00:03:43.930 --> 00:03:50.870
me do the dishes when we were first married no it was before that once when my parents invited you

00:03:50.870 --> 00:04:00.000
over for supper you practically ordered my mother out of the kitchen then you held my hands under the soap suds really was I ever

00:04:00.000 --> 00:04:09.190
that naive and callow? You thought it was very Robert Montgomery at the time. Ouch. Speaking of

00:04:09.190 --> 00:04:14.630
young romance, I wish Wally could take Kitty to that dance on Saturday. You know, Margaret's looking

00:04:14.630 --> 00:04:20.030
forward to it, and I hate to disappoint her. Honey, don't you think you could talk him into going?

00:04:20.540 --> 00:04:25.720
Well, dear, if he has a basketball practice, he can't let the team down. Well, you think it

00:04:25.720 --> 00:04:30.000
shows very good manners for a boy to put basketball ahead of girls? Well, no.

00:04:30.000 --> 00:04:33.180
- No, not good manners, but a solid sense of values.

00:04:41.160 --> 00:04:44.080
- You really doing homework, Wally?

00:04:44.080 --> 00:04:46.350
- Yeah, I'm really doing my homework.

00:04:46.350 --> 00:04:50.360
- But you did not really want dessert tonight, did ya?

00:04:50.360 --> 00:04:53.980
- Well, maybe I didn't really not want dessert tonight.

00:04:53.980 --> 00:04:55.090
What about it?

00:04:55.090 --> 00:04:56.170
- You wanted to get away from talking

00:04:56.170 --> 00:05:00.000
about that kiddie girl, didn't ya?

00:05:00.000 --> 00:05:02.440
- Beaver, it's bad enough I got a kid brother,

00:05:02.440 --> 00:05:03.900
but you don't have to go and make it worse

00:05:03.900 --> 00:05:06.500
by being right all the time.

00:05:06.500 --> 00:05:10.190
- What's wrong with Kitty Bannerman outside of being a girl?

00:05:10.190 --> 00:05:12.200
- Look, Beaver, if I tell you,

00:05:12.200 --> 00:05:14.450
you promise you won't tell anybody?

00:05:14.450 --> 00:05:15.310
- Well, sure.

00:05:15.310 --> 00:05:19.990
Cross my heart and hope to never see television again.

00:05:19.990 --> 00:05:20.610
- Okay.

00:05:33.420 --> 00:05:35.620
This is why I can't go out with Kitty Bannerman.

00:05:36.620 --> 00:05:39.210
Gee, they just look like letters.

00:05:39.660 --> 00:05:40.600
They are letters.

00:05:41.030 --> 00:05:42.510
They're letters from Kitty Bannerman.

00:05:42.830 --> 00:05:43.460
How come?

00:05:43.700 --> 00:05:45.820
She moved away from here three or four years ago.

00:05:47.490 --> 00:05:50.730
Well, the how come is that last summer when I was up at camp,

00:05:51.140 --> 00:05:53.580
some of the big shots up there were getting letters from girls

00:05:53.580 --> 00:05:54.660
and reading them out loud.

00:05:56.120 --> 00:05:58.390
Well, I guess I wanted to be a big shot, too.

00:05:58.590 --> 00:06:00.000
You mean you owe junk to this Kitty?

00:06:00.000 --> 00:06:01.280
and she wrote junk back to you?

00:06:01.890 --> 00:06:03.770
Yeah, and I laid it on real thick,

00:06:04.080 --> 00:06:05.620
so she'd really think I was something.

00:06:06.570 --> 00:06:07.820
