Takes care of the car. What about the tuxedo?

00:16:50.270 --> 00:16:52.270
Oh, well, I got a P.S. in here.

00:16:53.320 --> 00:16:59.620
P.S. It is okay if you wear one of your expensive evening dresses, but I will have to wear my blue suit.

00:17:00.350 --> 00:17:04.670
My mother loaned my tuxedo to a friend of Frank Sinatra's who spilled something on it.

00:17:06.030 --> 00:17:07.770
Yours truly, Wally Cleaver.

00:17:10.750 --> 00:17:12.110
Well, what do you think of it, Beef?

00:17:12.610 --> 00:17:13.870
What do you think of it, Wally?

00:17:15.040 --> 00:17:18.140
I think it's the craziest thing I ever read.

00:17:19.200 --> 00:17:21.710
So do I.

00:17:24.240 --> 00:17:24.580
Yeah.

00:17:24.840 --> 00:17:29.360
What are you going to do now?

00:17:30.220 --> 00:17:32.220
Well, I'm just gonna write her a regular note

00:17:32.220 --> 00:17:34.100
saying I'll be happy to take her to the dance.

00:17:34.860 --> 00:17:36.580
I hope I croak before Saturday night.

00:17:37.880 --> 00:17:45.920
Party for rich people.

00:17:46.940 --> 00:17:48.060
Smashed up my car.

00:17:49.020 --> 00:17:50.420
My father, a bank president.

00:17:52.010 --> 00:17:54.070
You say you found this in Wally's waistbasket?

00:17:54.730 --> 00:17:56.090
Yes, and there's something in there

00:17:56.090 --> 00:17:57.670
about loaning his tuxedo.

00:17:58.560 --> 00:18:00.000
Now, I know he never mailed

00:18:00.000 --> 00:18:05.300
it but why in the world would he write anything like that now wait a minute dear i think i'm

00:18:05.300 --> 00:18:10.790
beginning to put this whole thing together somehow wally gave this kitty bannerman the idea that he's

00:18:10.790 --> 00:18:16.660
a a lot more of a big time operator than he really is you know a sort of a junior playboy complete

00:18:16.660 --> 00:18:22.810
with his own car tuxedo rich father and everything i think he did mention riding her this summer

00:18:23.510 --> 00:18:29.000
but what why in the world would wally get himself way out on a limb like this for a girl

00:18:30.000 --> 00:18:36.950
that's the easiest thing in the world for any male to do when you talk to Wally

00:18:36.950 --> 00:18:43.040
would you try to let him know you're on his side yeah I'll try dear sometimes

00:18:43.040 --> 00:18:48.050
it's a little difficult to convince your son that you're really on his side

00:18:48.050 --> 00:18:54.850
she did I didn't think you and mom would find that letter well Wally that's a

00:18:54.850 --> 00:19:00.000
little beside the point now look son I'm trying to help you now you

00:19:00.000 --> 00:19:03.220
You say you wrote her six or seven letters this summer, huh?

00:19:03.220 --> 00:19:06.320
Yeah, and in each one of them, I made myself a bigger shot

00:19:06.320 --> 00:19:08.510
than the one before.

00:19:08.510 --> 00:19:09.850
Boy, the guys really thought I was something

00:19:09.850 --> 00:19:13.510
getting letters from a glamorous girl like Kitty.

00:19:13.510 --> 00:19:16.270
Well, Wally, all of us like to feel important,

00:19:16.270 --> 00:19:20.910
but I'm afraid you sort of went at this the wrong way.

00:19:20.910 --> 00:19:23.620
Have you figured a way out of it yet?

00:19:23.620 --> 00:19:26.190
Well, Eddie Haskell had a suggestion.

00:19:26.190 --> 00:19:27.530
What was it?

00:19:27.530 --> 00:19:30.000
Well, he said that if I drank about a quart of chocolate

00:19:30.000 --> 00:19:34.190
syrup and then a whole bottle of vinegar, I wouldn't be able to go to any dances for

00:19:34.190 --> 00:19:35.190
a couple weeks.

00:19:35.190 --> 00:19:36.190
I'm sorry.

00:19:36.190 --> 00:19:42.180
No, it's not easy, but I think you'd better just hope for the best and tell this girl

00:19:42.180 --> 00:19:45.500
the truth.

00:19:45.500 --> 00:19:50.530
But, gee, Dad, her father really does have a lot of money, and she has a couple fur coats

00:19:50.530 --> 00:19:56.190
and her own car, and she goes to parties with rich guys all the time, and if she finds out

00:19:56.190 --> 00:19:59.890
what I am tonight, she'll have everybody at the dance laughing at me.

00:20:00.190 --> 00:20:01.850
- It's too bad you didn't think of that, isn't it,

00:20:01.850 --> 00:20:06.130
before you pretended to be something you're not?

00:20:06.130 --> 00:20:10.060
- Okay, Dad, but Kitty and her mom

00:20:10.060 --> 00:20:12.140
are staying over to her grandparents for the weekend,

00:20:12.140 --> 00:20:16.190
and when you drive me over there to pick her up tonight,

00:20:16.190 --> 00:20:18.310
would you kinda do me a favor?

00:20:18.310 --> 00:20:19.240
- What is it?

00:20:19.240 --> 00:20:22.350
- Well, would you mind parking down the street a ways

00:20:22.350 --> 00:20:26.000
and kinda waiting out in the car for a couple minutes?

00:20:26.000 --> 00:20:28.590
You know, so I can tell Kitty what a nothing I am

00:20:28.590 --> 00:20:30.000
without anybody being around.

00:20:31.790 --> 00:20:35.900
Son, if you want me to, I'll wait out in the car for 20 minutes.

00:20:36.890 --> 00:20:37.710
Gee, thanks, Dad.

00:20:42.420 --> 00:20:54.170
This is the Miller house, isn't it?

00:20:54.390 --> 00:20:55.150
Yes, it is.

00:20:58.100 --> 00:20:59.860
Then, uh, you must be Kitty?

00:21:00.350 --> 00:21:01.350
Yes.

00:21:02.810 --> 00:21:04.580
Well, hi. I'm Wally Cleaver.

00:21:04.580 --> 00:21:07.040
It's nice to see you again, Wally.

00:21:07.040 --> 00:21:12.070
Well, I thought maybe your mom would answer the door or something.

00:21:12.070 --> 00:21:15.310
Well, when I heard you drive up in your car, I got to the door first.

00:21:15.310 --> 00:21:24.500
Yeah. Look, Kitty, before we go to the country club, could I talk to you about something for a minute?

00:21:24.500 --> 00:21:27.920
Of course, Wally. Would you like to sit down?

00:21:27.920 --> 00:21:30.000
Yeah.

00:21:30.060 --> 00:21:33.080
- Sure, if it won't bend your dress or anything.

00:21:42.490 --> 00:21:46.640
- Before you start, could I say something first?

00:21:46.640 --> 00:21:48.830
- Yeah, sure.

00:21:48.830 --> 00:21:50.710
- I just want to tell you that,

00:21:50.710 --> 00:21:52.510
well, if you don't want to take me to the dance tonight,

00:21:52.510 --> 00:21:56.360
it's all right with me and I won't blame you in the least.

00:21:56.360 --> 00:21:57.170
- Hmm?

00:21:57.170 --> 00:22:00.000
- I know how disappointed you must be after all those letters

00:22:00.000 --> 00:22:02.500
I wrote not to see me in a glamorous evening gown

00:22:02.500 --> 00:22:05.300
with a mink stole and an expensive hairdo and everything,

00:22:05.300 --> 00:22:07.970
like the girls you're used to going out with.

00:22:07.970 --> 00:22:09.170
But, gee, Kitty, I...

00:22:09.170 --> 00:22:10.970
I shouldn't have written you all those silly letters

00:22:10.970 --> 00:22:13.440
with all that romantic talk and everything.

00:22:13.440 --> 00:22:15.510
But after you told me how popular you were

00:22:15.510 --> 00:22:17.210
and how rich and everything,

00:22:17.210 --> 00:22:19.720
and how you and your folks knew all those celebrities,

00:22:19.720 --> 00:22:21.290
I just couldn't resist getting letters

00:22:21.290 --> 00:22:25.290
from such a glamorous, exciting boy.

00:22:25.290 --> 00:22:27.290
Holy mackerel.

00:22:27.290 --> 00:22:29.600
That picture I sent you wasn't me at all.

00:22:30.000 --> 00:22:37.760
my older sister it's that as i said if you're ashamed to take me to the country club to meet

00:22:37.760 --> 00:22:47.190
all your wealthy friends i'll understand blame me for laughing at me oh gee kitty i'm not laughing

00:22:47.190 --> 00:22:53.430
at you it's it's just that i'm so happy about what you just said that i don't know what to say

00:22:54.180 --> 00:23:00.000
happy yeah you see i don't have any rich friends or or i don't have a car or a

00:23:00.000 --> 00:23:04.150
a tuxedo or my father isn't the president of any bank.

00:23:04.150 --> 00:23:05.350
You know something else?

00:23:05.350 --> 00:23:06.170
- What?

00:23:06.170 --> 00:23:09.050
- If Frank Sinatra ever said hello to my mother,

00:23:09.050 --> 00:23:12.030
she'd probably have to go to bed for a couple weeks.

00:23:12.030 --> 00:23:14.500
- Your letters were just as phony as mine?

00:23:14.500 --> 00:23:17.320
- Boy, I'll say they were.

00:23:17.320 --> 00:23:18.940
- Wally, I've been worrying all week

00:23:18.940 --> 00:23:20.720
because I thought this would be the worst evening

00:23:20.720 --> 00:23:23.270
in my life, but now I have the feeling

00:23:23.270 --> 00:23:24.910
it might be one of the nicest.

00:23:26.750 --> 00:23:30.000
- You know, I kind of got that same feeling

00:23:30.000 --> 00:23:36.870
myself you said you didn't have a car Wally is that one of your friends out

00:23:36.870 --> 00:23:43.150
there waiting to drive us to the dance you know I never thought much about it

00:23:43.150 --> 00:23:47.570
before but I guess he's probably one of the best friends I got

00:24:12.640 --> 00:24:14.280
- You're a real sneaky one.

00:24:14.280 --> 00:24:15.840
You'd make a real neat burglar.

00:24:18.330 --> 00:24:21.270
- Beaver, you're not supposed to be awake this late.

00:24:21.270 --> 00:24:24.300
- Well, I was asleep, and I was dreaming I was awake,

00:24:24.300 --> 00:24:26.990
so I figured I might as well be awake.

00:24:26.990 --> 00:24:28.770
Stayed for the whole dance?

00:24:28.770 --> 00:24:29.800
- Well, sure I did.

00:24:30.440 --> 00:24:33.900
Gee, I thought when that girl found out you were nothing, she might sock you or something.

00:24:35.090 --> 00:24:38.010
Nobody socked anybody. I had a real good time.

00:24:38.490 --> 00:24:38.950
You did?

00:24:40.240 --> 00:24:44.860
Well, sure. Everything turned out great on account of she turned out to be a nothing, too.

00:24:45.720 --> 00:24:51.410
Yeah, she was writing those goofy letters the same way I was.

00:24:52.020 --> 00:24:53.760
She just wanted to be a big shot, too.

00:24:55.570 --> 00:24:57.910
You know, Wally, I've been thinking.

00:24:58.520 --> 00:24:58.780
Yeah?

00:25:00.000 --> 00:25:01.960
Girls aren't so different from boys after all.

00:25:40.840 --> 00:25:44.760
Thank you.
